    text_index_char_int_context_warning_to_error_2026-11-03, 0, "2026-11-10 Fable fix lane (work/p2-textidx-char-error): the 'warning' this row was meant to promote never existed in the pure-Simple compiler. 30.types already infers text[i] as Char (type_infer/inference_expr.spl), but no checker diagnostic covered a char reaching an integer context; only the lexical guard scripts/check/check-string-index-char-to-i64.shs did (census 2026-11-10: PASS, 765 sites scanned, 0 string-indexed .to_i64() hits in src/lib). Implemented the staged diagnostic W-CHAR-INT-CONTEXT / E-CHAR-INT-CONTEXT in HIR lowering, mirroring W-CHAR-CONDITION: arithmetic (+ - * / %) with a char operand (declared char, or a non-range index on a text base), and the integer-parse conversions (to_i64/to_int/to_i32/to_u8/to_u32/to_u64/to_f64) on a char receiver. `+` is flagged only against a known-integer other side (int literal, int-typed symbol, or arithmetic subterm, so h * 31 + s[i] is caught) because + is also text concat. Silent: .ord(), as i64, .to_digit(), char comparisons, char_code_at/byte_at, s[a..b]. Mode precedence SIMPLE_SAFETY_PROFILE=critical|verified > SIMPLE_CHAR_INT_CONTEXT=error|warn > ci_default_mode(). Files: src/compiler/20.hir/exhaustiveness/char_int_context.spl (new), hir_lowering/statements.spl (check_char_int_binary/check_char_int_method/report_char_int_context), hir_lowering/_Expressions/expression_core.spl (Binary arm + both MethodCall arms). Spec test/01_unit/compiler/hir/char_int_context_spec.spl: red 0/16 executed (module absent) -> green 16/16; sibling char_condition_spec.spl stays 16/16. Scoped error landed: E-CHAR-INT-CONTEXT is fatal under SIMPLE_CHAR_INT_CONTEXT=error and under critical/verified profiles. The DEFAULT flip (ci_default_mode() warn -> error, one switch point) stays blocked on the ADR-005 promotion trigger: phase 3 (stage3 self-build) has not passed and Windows/macOS/Linux self-hosted binaries are not all admitted. Flip when that gate opens; the spec's promotion-gate example pins the switch."
